///////////CINE - OUTRO 03 /////////////

SCRIPT:mgfotr_aragorn270A
"Aragorn: Halbarad, my truest friend. For you to fall when the aim for which you fought was so near is a grievous hurt."
End

SCRIPT:mgfotr_aragorn270B
"Aragorn: Be at peace, son of Arnor."
End

///////////CINE - OUTRO 04 /////////////

SCRIPT:mgfotr_faramir079
"Faramir: The Heir of Elendil has come forth, father. To refuse him would bring dishonour upon our House.\nIt is by the leadership of Aragorn that the Enemy has been repelled."
End

SCRIPT:mgfotr_faramir080
"Faramir: We have little time."
End

SCRIPT:mgfotr_denethor056
"Denethor: What say you of this, Boromir?"
End

SCRIPT:mgfotr_denethor057
"Denethor: Leave me. I require time and silence to examine the meaning of these events."
End

SCRIPT:mgfotr_denethor058
"Denethor: The time of my thought is yet mine to spend, Faramir!"
End

SCRIPT:mgfotr_boromir041
"Boromir: This is a time to rejoice, father. Turning Aragorn away would invite chaos amongst our ranks.\nThis war is not over, and we must press our advantage whilst we can."
End

///////////CINE - OUTRO 05 /////////////

SCRIPT:mgfotr_denethor059
"Denethor: It is due to Boromir's counsel that I have come to realise what must be done."
End

SCRIPT:mgfotr_denethor060
"Denethor: Today, I must render unto thee not merely lordship of my lands, but also of my people,\nwhose lives and well-being are near to my heart."
End

SCRIPT:mgfotr_aragorn245
"Aragorn: Hail, Lord Denethor, Steward of Gondor. A star shines upon the hour of our meeting."
End

SCRIPT:mgfotr_aragorn246A
"Aragorn: The House of Stewards has long seen to the survival of Gondor. Though I will take up kingship over you,\nI wish for you to remain at your post, and defend Minas Tirith in my absence."
End

SCRIPT:mgfotr_aragorn246B
"Aragorn: Only together do we have a chance at victory."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_gondorsoldier036
"Gondor Soldier: Lord Eomer of Rohan! Your sister has been taken to the Houses of Healing. She yet lives,\nbut is near death! You must go to her at once!"
End

SCRIPT:mgfotr_eomer051
"Eomer: Eowyn!"
End

///////////CINE - OUTRO 06 /////////////

SCRIPT:mgfotr_aragorn247
"Aragorn: This City and realm has rested in the charge of the Stewards for many long years,\nand I will not make any claim until it is seen whether we or Mordor shall prevail."
End

SCRIPT:mgfotr_aragorn248
"Aragorn: No. But I deem the time unripe, and I have no mind for strife except with our Enemy and his servants.\nI will await the welcome of the Lord of the City."
End

SCRIPT:mgfotr_eomer049
"Eomer: You have raised the king's banner and displayed the tokens of Elendil's House.\nWill you suffer these to be challenged?"
End

SCRIPT:mgfotr_imrahil017
"Imrahil: Your words are wise, lord. But I would not have you remain like a beggar at the door."
End

SCRIPT:mgfotr_gandalf251A
"Gandalf: He must not."
End

SCRIPT:mgfotr_gandalf251B
"Gandalf: Denethor is no more. His son, now Steward, lies gravely wounded at the Houses of Healing."
End

SCRIPT:mgfotr_gandalf251C
"Gandalf: Eomer, your sister is there also. She yet lives, but is near death. Go to her!"
End

SCRIPT:mgfotr_gandalf252
"Gandalf: The hands of the king are the hands of a healer, and so shall the rightful king be known.\nCome, Aragorn. You are needed."
End

///////////CINE - OUTRO 07 /////////////

SCRIPT:mgfotr_boromir042
"Boromir: Nor the courage of Gondor."
End

SCRIPT:mgfotr_aragorn458
"Aragorn: We have come now to the very brink. To waver is to fall. We must march upon the Black Gate,\nto draw out Sauron's armies and give Frodo what time we can."
End

SCRIPT:mgfotr_eomer050
"Eomer: I know little of these deep matters. But you came to our rescue, and if you go, I will follow."
End

SCRIPT:mgfotr_imrahil018
"Imrahil: Then you would have us retreat to our castles and await our doom?"
End

SCRIPT:mgfotr_imrahil019
"Imrahil: Nor the courage of Gondor."
End

SCRIPT:mgfotr_gandalf253
"Gandalf: At great cost have we survived the first assault. The next will be greater.\nPrudence would counsel you to strengthen what strong places remain to you."
End

SCRIPT:mgfotr_gandalf429
"Gandalf: No, for I do not counsel prudence. I believe that we must place our hope in the destruction of the Ring of Power."
End

SCRIPT:mgfotr_legolas138
"Legolas: We have come this far, Aragorn. We are with you."
End

SCRIPT:mgfotr_gimli136
"Gimli: Aye. Let none doubt the steadfastness of Durin's Folk."
End

///////////CINE - OUTRO 08/////////////

SCRIPT:mgfotr_legolas139
"Legolas: Your kinsmen may have no need to ride to war; I fear war already marches on their own lands."
End

SCRIPT:mgfotr_gimli137
"Gimli: I wish I could summon some of our own kinsfolk south. A contingent of stout Dwarves, eager for battle."
End

